{"name":"Cabo","hex":"#cec0aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cabo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Abbreviation of Cabo San Lucas: a resort city in Baja California Sur, Mexico."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cabo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cabo San Lucas","blocks":[{"text":"Cabo San Lucas, also known simply as Cabo, is a resort city at the southern tip of the Baja California peninsula, in the Mexican state of Baja California Sur. As of the 2020 Census, the population of the city was 202,694. Cabo San Lucas and the neighboring San José del Cabo are collectively known as Los Cabos. Together, they form a metropolitan area of 351,111 inhabitants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Collage_Cabo_San_Lucas.jpg/330px-Collage_Cabo_San_Lucas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabo_San_Lucas","wikidata":"Q1020776"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Escudo_Cabo_San_Lucas.gif/120px-Escudo_Cabo_San_Lucas.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/16/Escudo_Cabo_San_Lucas.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Escudo_Cabo_San_Lucas.gif/120px-Escudo_Cabo_San_Lucas.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEscudo_Cabo_San_Lucas.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Cabo_San_Lucas_Los_Arcos_3.jpg/500px-Cabo_San_Lucas_Los_Arcos_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Cabo_San_Lucas_Los_Arcos_3.jpg/1280px-Cabo_San_Lucas_Los_Arcos_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&